<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Intentionally empty today.

	  Sign in with Apple is a real App Store requirement for this app (it
	  offers Google sign-in on web), but it is BLOCKED server-side: the
	  backend registers Apple only as a NextAuth *web* OAuth provider
	  using a Services ID, and no route accepts a native
	  ASAuthorizationAppleIDCredential identityToken and returns a mobile
	  session token. See "B2. Sign in with Apple (native)" in
	  ios-native/PARITY.md for the exact contract that route needs.

	  Declaring the entitlement before that route exists would demand a
	  provisioning profile carrying a capability the app cannot yet use,
	  and would break automatic signing for anyone whose team has not
	  enabled it. When B2 is unblocked, add:

	      <key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	      <array><string>Default</string></array>

	  and enable "Sign in with Apple" for one.zrp.social in the developer
	  portal at the same time.

	  Push notifications (aps-environment) are likewise deferred to Phase
	  11 and are blocked on B3 - see PARITY.md.

	  Universal links are the third: DeepLink.swift maps every ZRP web
	  path this app has a screen for, ZRPSocialApp receives them through
	  onOpenURL, and the tab shell opens them - that half is done and is
	  already used for zrp.one links tapped inside a post. What is
	  missing is entirely outside the code:

	      <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	      <array><string>applinks:zrp.one</string></array>

	  plus public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association naming
	  "TEAMID.one.zrp.social". The Team ID does not exist yet - there is
	  no Apple Developer account for this app - and an invented one would
	  produce a file Apple silently refuses to honour, which is worse
	  than no file at all. Android's equivalent
	  (public/.well-known/assetlinks.json) is real because its signing
	  certificate exists.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
